#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:7
msgid "Debugging Syncthing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:9
msgid ""
"There's a lot that happens behind the covers, and Syncthing is generally "
"quite silent about it. A number of environment variables can be used to set "
"the logging to verbose for various parts of the program, and to enable "
"profiling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:15
msgid "Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:18
msgid "STTRACE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:20
msgid ""
"The environment variable ``STTRACE`` can be set to a comma separated list of "
"\"facilities\", to enable extra debugging information for said facility. A "
"facility generally maps to a Go package, although there are a few extra that "
"map to parts of the ``main`` package. Currently, the following facilities "
"are supported (an up to date list is always printed by ``syncthing --help``):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:27
msgid "``beacon`` (the beacon package)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:28
msgid "``discover`` (the discover package)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:29
msgid "``events`` (the events package)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:30
msgid "``files`` (the files package)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:31
msgid "``http`` (the main package; HTTP requests)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:32
msgid "``net`` (the main package; connections & network messages)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:33
msgid "``model`` (the model package)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:34
msgid "``scanner`` (the scanner package)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:35
msgid "``stats`` (the stats package)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:36
msgid "``upnp`` (the upnp package)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:37
msgid "``xdr`` (the xdr package)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:38
msgid "``all`` (all of the above)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:40
msgid ""
"The debug output is often of the kind that it doesn't make much sense "
"without looking at the code. The purpose of the different packages / "
"facilities are something like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:44
msgid ""
"``beacon`` sends and receives UDP broadcasts used by the local discovery "
"system. Debugging here will show which interfaces and addresses are selected "
"for broadcasts, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:47
msgid ""
"``discover`` sends and receives local discovery packets. Debugging here will "
"output the parsed packets, nodes that get registered etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:49
msgid ""
"``files`` keeps track of lists of files with metadata and figures out which "
"is the newest version of each."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:51
msgid ""
"``net`` shows connection attempts, incoming connections, and the low level "
"error when connection attempts fail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:53
msgid ""
"``model`` is the largest chunk of the system; this is where pulling of out "
"of date files happens, indexes are sent and received, and incoming requests "
"for file chunks are logged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:56
msgid ""
"``scanner`` is the local filesystem scanner. Debugging here will output "
"information about changed and unchanged files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:58
msgid "``upnp`` is the upnp talker."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:59
msgid ""
"``xdr`` is the low level protocol encoder. Debugging here will output all "
"bytes sent/received over the sync connection. Very verbose."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:61
msgid "``all`` simply enables debugging of all facilities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:63
msgid ""
"Enabling any of the facilities will also change the log format to include "
"microsecond timestamps and file names plus line numbers. This can be used to "
"enable this extra information on the normal logging level, without enabling "
"any debugging: ``STTRACE=somethingnonexistent`` for example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:69
msgid ""
"Under Unix (including Mac) the easiest way to run Syncthing with an "
"environment variable set is to prepend the variable to the command line. I.e:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:73
msgid "``$ STTRACE=model syncthing``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:75
msgid "On windows, it needs to be set prior to running Syncthing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:79
msgid ""
"C:\\> set STTRACE=model\n"
"C:\\> syncthing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:83
msgid "STPROFILER"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:85
msgid ""
"The ``STPROFILER`` environment variable sets the listen address for the HTTP "
"profiler. If set to for example ``:9090`` the profiler will start and listen "
"on port 9090. http://localhost:9090/debug/pprof is then the address to the "
"profiler. Se ``go tool pprof`` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:91
msgid "STGUIASSETS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:93
msgid ""
"Directory to load GUI assets from. Overrides compiled in assets. Useful for "
"developing webgui, commonly use ``STGUIASSETS=gui bin/syncthing``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:97
msgid "STCPUPROFILE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:99
msgid "Write a CPU profile to ``cpu-$pid.pprof`` on exit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:102
msgid "STHEAPPROFILE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:104
msgid ""
"Write heap profiles to ``heap-$pid-$timestamp.pprof`` each time heap usage "
"increases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:108
msgid "STBLOCKPROFILE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:110
msgid ""
"Write block profiles to ``block-$pid-$timestamp.pprof`` every 20 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:114
msgid "STPERFSTATS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:116
msgid ""
"Write running performance statistics to ``perf-$pid.csv``. Not supported on "
"Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:120
msgid "STNOUPGRADE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:122
msgid "Disable automatic upgrades."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:125
msgid "GOMAXPROCS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:127
msgid ""
"Set the maximum number of CPU cores to use. Defaults to all available CPU "
"cores."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:131
msgid "GOGC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/debugging.rst:133
msgid ""
"Percentage of heap growth at which to trigger GC. Default is 100. Lower "
"numbers keep peak memory usage down, at the price of CPU usage (ie. "
"performance)"
msgstr ""
